    "details": "NLnet Labs reports:\n\n> This release consolidates security fixes for issues reported over a\n> period of time. There are fixes for:\n>\n> - CVE-2026-33278: Possible remote code execution during DNSSEC\n>   validation.\n> - CVE-2026-42944: Heap overflow and crash with multiple nsid, cookie,\n>   padding EDNS options.\n> - CVE-2026-42959: Crash during DNSSEC validation of malicious content.\n> - CVE-2026-32792: Packet of death with DNSCrypt.\n> - CVE-2026-40622: \\\"Ghost domain name\\\" variant.\n> - CVE-2026-41292: Parsing a long list of incoming EDNS options\n>   degrades performance.\n> - CVE-2026-42534: Jostle logic bypass degrades resolution performance.\n> - CVE-2026-42923: Degradation of service with unbounded NSEC3 hash\n>   calculations.\n> - CVE-2026-42960: Possible cache poisoning attack while following\n>   delegation.\n> - CVE-2026-44390: Unbounded name compression in certain cases causes\n>   degradation of service.\n> - CVE-2026-44608: Use after free and crash in RPZ code.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0244",
